SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE

The MIT license above covers the source code and documentation of this
repository only: src/, scripts/, docs/, tests/, and the project configuration
files (pyproject.toml, requirements.txt).

The data/ directory is not uniform. The following terms apply.

1. data/corpora/ and data/results/ -- MIT.

   The 600 source sentences in data/corpora/ are author-created original
   text. The CSVs in data/results/ contain derived metric values (BLEU, TER,
   cosine and embedding scores) computed from those sentences. Both are the
   author's own work and both are covered by the MIT license above.

2. data/translation_cache.json.gz -- NOT MIT.

   This file is machine-translation output rather than author-created work,
   and is not the author's to relicense. It holds 141,088 unique cached
   translations:

   * 69,962 entries produced by Google Translate. Use of this output is
     subject to Google's Terms of Service.

   * 71,126 entries produced by NLLB-200
     (facebook/nllb-200-distilled-600M). NLLB-200 is released under
     CC-BY-NC 4.0, which permits non-commercial research use only. Output
     generated with the model carries that restriction.

   The file is committed solely for reproducibility: it lets anyone verify
   the published results without re-issuing 162,000 translation operations
   against either system. It is not offered as a redistributable translation
   dataset.

COMMERCIAL USE

The code, corpora and results are available for commercial use under the MIT
license above. The translation cache is not. To use this project
commercially, delete data/translation_cache.json.gz and regenerate it under
your own licensed access to a translation system, using the runners in
scripts/ -- see "Reproducing the experiments" in README.md. The regenerated
cache is then yours under whatever terms that access grants you.

See the "License" section of README.md for the same breakdown in prose.
